       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the usual maximum dose, so I need you to confirm what you meant before anything goes in.\n\n- **Usual adult dosing:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily and increase as needed. The maximum is 200 mg/day.\n- **What 1000 mg could mean:** this amount is in the overdose range and carries a real risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures and heart rhythm problems (QT prolongation).\n- **Possible typo:** it may be an extra zero, and 100 mg was intended. 100 mg once daily is a common maintenance dose.\n\nCould you tell me the dose you want? For example:\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg** by mouth, once daily\n2. **Sertraline 50 mg** by mouth, once daily (a typical starting dose if the patient is new to sertraline)\n3. Another dose of your choice\n\nI'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
